      <p class="note">The same rule is used for prediction and chronological backtesting. Model MAE: ${fmt(r.mae)}; prior-week baseline MAE: ${fmt(r.baseline)} adjusted days. ${r.ok&&r.folds>=3?(r.mae<r.baseline?"Lower synthetic historical error does not establish clinical validity.":"The rule did not outperform the prior-week baseline."):"Too few folds or no projection; no reliable performance comparison."}</p>
      <p class="note">Shading uses 1.5 × MAE, with a 1–3-day half-width. It is a heuristic range, not a confidence interval or calibrated uncertainty estimate. Reporting bias, confounding, and serial dependence are not corrected. The horizon follows the dataset cutoff, not today's date.</p>
